## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/services/oauth_deep_link_router.dart | ⚠️ important the replay buffer has no lifetime binding — stale callbacks replay into unrelated later flows and fail them with a state mismatch buffer line 62 retains any fah oauth network link delivered while no flow is registered and register line 69 replays it to the next flow that binds — with no check that the link belongs to that flow verified in this review with a scratch test removed afterwards after dispatching a cold start callback while no route lives deeplinkoauthreceiver bindwithrouter resolves receiver callback with the stale uri — scratch resolved with fah oauth network code old state s old reachable trace 1 cold start on the oauth callback boot dispatches the launch link twice stream getinitiallink → 2 copies buffered the resume path resumeoauthsigninfrominitiallink network session manager dart 209 241 exchanges the code directly and never registers a receiver so the buffered copies are never drained 2 the next manual sign in auth flow dart 88 signin → startreceiver → bindwithrouter replays the stale link → state initiated state auth flow dart 109 → authflowexception sign in state mismatch — the callback did not come from this flow → the attempt dies before the user s real callback arrives 3 the loop repeats each failed attempt close s unregisters its own real browser callback then lands with no route → buffered → poisons the next attempt manual sign in keeps failing until process restart a second trigger is new in this pr a callback delivered on the stream while no flow lives e g a late redirect after a timed out closed attempt used to be dropped it is now buffered and replays into the next attempt also verified with the scratch test to be fair the primary loop is pre existing on main too app links never clears the native initiallink so the old bindwithinitiallink completed fresh flows from the stale launch link the same way — but the pr rearchitects exactly this pipeline and its stated contract replayed exactly once to the first route that claims it ships without ownership or liveness checks and without a test for stale replay into later flow fix directions author s call give buffered links a ttl aligned with the pending oauth freshness window the 3 minute flow timeout and or have the successful cold start resume drain the buffer it just consumed please also add a test pinning a buffered link from a dead attempt must not complete a later flow |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | flutter_app/lib/services/oauth_deep_link_router.dart | ⚠️ important unknown route logging persists live oauth code state to logs app log line 96 logs the full uri — query string included dart applog i tag no route for oauth deep link uri applog i appends to the 200 line in memory ring buffer and persists to logs app log 1 mb tail app log dart 4 8 which the settings screen s copy debug logs surfaces — so oauth credentials can end up in logs users paste for support this is not limited to junk links on ios no network route ever registers the flow uses webauthsessionoauthreceiver auth loopback io dart 190 206 which never touches the router while the app registers the bare fah scheme — no filtering auth deep link dart 74 77 — and the os delivers engine side copies of fah oauth network main dart 150 156 every such copy is therefore an unknown route here the real code state gets logged verbatim and buffered never drained see the sibling thread on main the boot listener silently dropped non openrouter links fix log only the path — applog i tag no route for oauth deep link uri path the log once dedup key at line 95 is already uri path so nothing diagnostic is lost and credentials stay out of persisted logs |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | flutter_app/lib/services/oauth_deep_link_router.dart | 💡 suggestion loggedunknownpaths grows unbounded for the process lifetime the buffer right above it is deliberately bounded bufferlimit oldest dropped but the log once dedup set string line 63 has no cap every distinct unknown fah oauth path adds an entry that is never removed on ios the bare fah scheme is registered with no path filter so any web page location href fah oauth … or app can inject links with arbitrary distinct paths each one grows the set in memory only and reset on restart so this is not urgent — but the inconsistency bounded buffer unbounded dedup is worth closing with the same bounded queue pattern e g keep the last n seen paths |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: baf1ea4c22d54db9b5b8d74e9b32fbfe4366d9eb
Current head: 083cb9e49c5e5f34bd808e641f9375d75a204c79

