Author: ai.teammate <agent.ai.native@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 25 16:26:52 2026 +0200

    fix(2395): pre-arrival ownership — replayed callbacks can no longer fail a later flow

    Root fix for the stale-replay poison loop: the router's replay now lands
    in the receiver's PRE-ARRIVAL slot instead of completing the callback.
    NetworkAuthFlow state-checks the slot right after initiate: a matching
    pre-arrival answers the flow directly (browser handoff skipped); a
    mismatched one is a dead attempt's callback — discarded as noise while
    the flow waits for its own live callback, whose state mismatch stays
    fatal (CSRF guard intact). Buffer entries are additionally time-bounded
    (replayTtl = the 3-minute flow-timeout envelope, injectable clock), the
    unknown-route log line carries scheme/host/path only (no code+state into
    logs/app.log), and the unknown-path dedup set is capped.

